# Implementation Plan — Internationalization (i18n) with react-i18next

Localize TableNova into **English (en)**, **Vietnamese (vi)** and **Japanese (ja)**.

Delivered in phases. **Phase 1 is implemented**; phase 2 and 3 are the remaining scope.

## Libraries

Already present in `package.json` and installed:

- **`i18next`** `^26.3.6`
- **`react-i18next`** `^17.0.11`
- **`i18next-browser-languagedetector`** `^8.2.1`

---

## Decisions

These were settled before writing code; they are the reason the file layout looks the way it does.

| Topic | Decision |
|---|---|
| Fallback | `fallbackLng: 'en'` (single value, not "vi / en"). |
| Detection | `order: ['localStorage', 'navigator']` only. Querystring/cookie detection is **off** — the app already uses a query param of its own (`?term=`) for the terminal window. |
| Storage key | `tf_lang`, matching the existing `tf_theme` / `tf_default_profile_id` convention. |
| Locale resolution | `supportedLngs` + `nonExplicitSupportedLngs: true`, so `ja-JP` / `vi-VN` from `navigator` resolve to `ja` / `vi` instead of dropping to the fallback. |
| Loading | Dictionaries are **bundled**, not fetched — the app must work offline (same reason fonts are vendored). `react.useSuspense: false`; there is nothing to suspend on. |
| Key type-safety | `vi.ts` / `ja.ts` are typed `typeof en`, and `i18next.d.ts` augments `CustomTypeOptions`. A missing key or a typo in `t('…')` is a **build error**, not a raw key rendered at runtime. |
| Plurals | Placeholders are named `{{n}}`, never `{{count}}` — `count` switches i18next into plural mode and would require `_one`/`_other` siblings per language, breaking flat key parity. |
| Inline markup | Strings with emphasis go through `<Trans>` with `<strong>` / `<code>` tags so each language controls word order around the emphasised part. |
| Vietnamese comments | Unchanged. The CLAUDE.md convention covers **comments**; only user-facing **strings** moved into `vi.ts`, verbatim, so the Vietnamese UI reads exactly as before. |
| CJK fonts | Inter and JetBrains Mono carry no CJK glyphs. `--win-font-sans` / `--win-font-mono` gained OS CJK fallbacks (Yu Gothic UI / Hiragino Sans / Noto Sans JP / Meiryo). These are system fonts, never fetched — offline rendering is preserved. |

