## Phase 1 — Infrastructure + connection & navigation surfaces (DONE)

### `src/i18n/`

- **`index.ts`** — i18next bootstrap with the config above. Exports `SUPPORTED_LANGUAGES`, `LANGUAGE_STORAGE_KEY` and `currentLanguage()`. Keeps `<html lang>` in sync on `languageChanged` so the browser picks the right CJK face and line-breaking rules.
- **`i18next.d.ts`** — `CustomTypeOptions` augmentation that makes `t()` key-aware.
- **`locales/en.ts`** — source of truth for the key tree.
- **`locales/vi.ts`**, **`locales/ja.ts`** — typed `typeof en`.
- **`__tests__/locales.test.ts`** — runtime guard for what types cannot see: empty values, dropped `{{…}}` placeholders, dropped `<Trans>` tags.

Namespaces so far: `common`, `language`, `titlebar`, `sidebar`, `createTable`, `connection`, `confirmDialog`.

### Wiring

- **`main.tsx`** — side-effect `import './i18n'` before the first render. Covers both the main window and the standalone terminal window (`?term=`), since both come through this entry.
- **`index.css`** — CJK fallbacks appended to the two font stacks.

### Localized components

- **`TitleBar.tsx`** — all menus + a **Language** menu (🇬🇧/🇻🇳/🇯🇵, check mark on the active one). Its category label is bilingual (`Language / 言語`) so a user staring at a UI they cannot read still finds it.
- **`Sidebar.tsx`** — database switcher, tools, table/function/procedure lists, context menu, and every rename/create/drop dialog.
- **`ConnectionManager.tsx`** — the full screen: profile list, all four DB forms, SSL and SSH tabs, AWS IAM block, Backup & Restore mode, and the URL-import / export / decrypt modals.
- **`CreateTableModal.tsx`**, **`ConfirmDialog.tsx`**.

### Notes for anyone extending this

- `t` shadowing: several `.map(t => …)` / `.find(t => …)` callbacks had to be renamed (`item`, `nt`, `tableName`) because `t` is now the translation function. Watch for this in the remaining files.
- Module-level helpers cannot call the hook. `formatRestoreEta()` takes `t` as its first argument; `SSL_MODE_DESC` / `LED_TITLE` became lookups inside the component. Dynamic keys (`t(\`a.${x}\`)`) defeat the typed key tree — use a `switch` instead.
- The mount-only bootstrap effect in `ConnectionManager` carries an `eslint-disable-next-line react-hooks/exhaustive-deps`: `t` changes identity on language change, and adding it to the deps would reload profiles and reset a half-filled form.

